questions.prompt:
Find the vulnerability and fix it:

```js
async function renderComments(postId) {
  const comments = await fetch('/api/posts/' + postId + '/comments').then(r => r.json());
  const list = document.getElementById('comments');
  for (const c of comments) {
    list.innerHTML += '<li><b>' + c.author + '</b>: ' + c.text + '</li>';
  }
}
```

What could an attacker do with it, and what additional defenses would you add?

questions.answer:
